.TH MEL 1 "2026" "mel 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mel \- a beautiful, customizable X11 screen locker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mel
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
mel covers every monitor with a fullscreen window, grabs keyboard and pointer, and unlocks after a successful PAM authentication. For dwm, use \fBxss-lock -- dwm --lock\fR to prepare the keyboard layout.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIfile\fR
Use a custom config file.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-layout " " \fIname\fR
minimal, card, left, pill, avatar, band, terminal, corner, ring, reactor, split, zen or horizon.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " " \fIname\fR
Select a colour theme; user config colours override the theme.
.TP
.B \-\-list-layouts
List available layouts and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-preview \fIfile.png\fR
Write a PNG without locking or authenticating. Blur and dim use a gradient.
.TP
.B \-\-preview-size \fIWIDTHxHEIGHT\fR
Preview size, from 320x240 to 4096x2160 (default 1280x720).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIpath\fR
Background image (PNG).
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-background " " \fImode\fR
blur, dim, image, solid or gradient.
.TP
.B \-\-blur \fIstrength\fR
Blur strength.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-fade
Disable animations.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mel/config, ~/.config/mel/config, /etc/mel.conf
.br
Themes: \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mel/themes/NAME\fR, \fI~/.config/mel/themes/NAME\fR, \fIPREFIX/share/mel/themes/NAME\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
xss-lock(1), pam(8)
